      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Express 4: wrap with `asyncHandler(fn)` or you leak.",
            "Express 5 forwards rejections to `next()` for you.",
            "Under PM2 / systemd / k8s, crash-and-restart is correct.",
            "Flush logs first, then `process.exit(1)`."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Cancellation Truth",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Promises cannot be cancelled — settling is permanent.",
            "Cancelling = tell the operation to stop, then reject.",
            "`AbortController` / `signal` is the standard mechanism."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const c = new AbortController();",
            "const r = fetch(url, { signal: c.signal });",
            "c.abort();   // fires 'abort', sets signal.aborted"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Accepts { signal }",
            "Since"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "fetch",
              "18"
            ],
            [
              "fs/promises reads",
              "15"
            ],
            [
              "events.once",
              "15"
            ],
            [
              "timers/promises",
              "15"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "AbortError is control flow",
          "text": "`err.name === 'AbortError'` means you cancelled it. Don't page anyone; don't count it as an app error."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Signals Kit",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const t = AbortSignal.timeout(5000);  // self-fires",
            "const s = AbortSignal.any([req.signal, t]);",
            "await fs.readFile(p, { signal: s });"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Timeout By Race",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const t = setTimeout(() => ctl.abort(), 5000);",
            "try { await work({ signal: ctl.signal }); }",
            "finally { clearTimeout(t); }  // or it hangs"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`race([work(), sleep(5000)])` works but leaks two ways.",
            "The loser keeps running; the timer keeps the loop alive.",
            "`timers/promises` setTimeout(ms, v, {signal}) is the fix.",
            "Cleanup in `finally`: connections, handles, listeners."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Shutdown & Error Context",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "SIGTERM: stop accepting, abort in-flight, drain, exit.",
            "Give the drain a hard deadline — then exit anyway."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
