          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const h = monitorEventLoopDelay();  // perf_hooks",
            "h.enable();",
            "report('loop_p99', h.percentile(99));"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Report p99 lag as a health metric, not a debug print.",
            "Leaked handles: `process.getActiveResourcesInfo()`.",
            "Or `why-is-node-running` when the process won't exit.",
            "`node --inspect` shows async stacks + pending microtasks."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "The silent bug",
          "text": "A forgotten `await`: the function returns a pending promise, callers read `undefined`, errors vanish. `no-floating-promises` + `require-await` catch most of them."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "await expect(fn()).rejects.toThrow(MyErr);",
            "jest.advanceTimersByTime(5000);",
            "// fake timers must advance or promises never settle"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Pick The Primitive",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Tool",
            "Wins",
            "Costs"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "callbacks",
              "no alloc, repeatable",
              "no compose, no catch"
            ],
            [
              "promises",
              "compose, settle once",
              "microtask + object"
            ],
            [
              "async/await",
              "readable, stacks",
              "hides parallelism"
            ],
            [
              "EventEmitter",
              "many values",
              "no backpressure"
            ],
            [
              "streams",
              "many + backpressure",
              "more API surface"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Debugging Async & Choosing The Tool",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One future value → promise.",
            "Many values over time → stream or async iterator.",
            "Recurring notifications → EventEmitter.",
            "EventEmitter needs an 'error' listener or it crashes."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Cost Model",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One `.then` step ≈ one microtask + one object.",
            "Millions of tiny promises show up as GC pressure.",
            "Batch hot loops instead of promising per item.",
            "CPU work: `worker_threads` (cheap) or `child_process`."
          ]
        },
